WEBVTT

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.150
I slept well.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.620
It's been a while since we slept in a nice, soft bed.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.820
Well Escha brought us here so the people are also very accommodating.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.570
We should thank her.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.070
What about the person with her?

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.450
Um...

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.270
What's his name again?

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.160
It's them.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.690
Have you two figured out why the water was stagnate?

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:05.540
Yes.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.480
We heard about it from the village chief.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.150
The water in this lake flows from upstream,

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.280
but since a while ago the flow of water has tapered off and sediment built up.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.630
That's why the lake's water looked so murky.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.490
Even though Escha-chan purified the water,

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.330
it's going to happen again, isn't it?

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.870
Is something wrong upstream?

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:33.540
Ruins?

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.780
Yeah.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:38.790
It seems the water originates there and flows down.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.690
Have the villagers gone to the ruins to investigate?

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.660
It seems they didn't go inside.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.770
Entering the ruins would be dangerous, after all.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.230
Dangerous...

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.900
That's right, that applies to us too.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.900
What's that?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.900
You're scared?

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.450
That's not it.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.130
Our mission is already complete.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.220
We've successfully resupplied the village.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.200
They won't have any problems with the water for now.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.280
All we have left to do is to report the situation to the branch.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:13.630
When I purified the water yesterday, the villagers were very thankful.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.720
"Thank you.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.470
If it had stayed that way, we would have needed to move out of the village."

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.970
"Thank you.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.930
Now we can stay in the village."

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:30.690
A Purify Bottle can't keep flowing water clean forever.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.560
It can't truly save this village either.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:36.190
I...

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:40.320
If there's really something that I can do,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.160
I'll do it no matter what it is.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.090
She's really just like her.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:47.830
That's right.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.000
So what are you going to do?

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:54.070
I-

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:55.050
I guess we can't help it.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.290
Once Escha makes a decision, she's not going to change her mind.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.510
Oh, is that so?

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.470
That's right.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:00.970
Now that you've made up your mind, let's go.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.010
Let's get to the ruins before it gets dark.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.470
Logy-san, thank you!

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:08.850
No need to thank me.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:11.560
Okay, let's get ready.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.560
Okay!

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.090
Nio?

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.360
You two don't have to follow us.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:29.810
You know, we were only allowed to stay in the village because they thought we were your companions.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.100
If we didn't follow you, they would think something's up.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.120
I see.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:36.790
Besides, she said she wanted to come too.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.960
I heard a voice.

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:47.760
Ever since coming to this region, I can sometimes hear a girl's voice.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:53.250
She speaks in bits and pieces, and I don't really understand what she's saying,

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.190
but the voices keep coming.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.690
And just now, I heard that voice again.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:00.860
What did she say?

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.330
"Stay away."

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.290
It's huge!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.000
This is completely different from yesterday's.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.070
This is...

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.280
It might be alive.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.070
Alive?

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.050
You'll understand once we go inside.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.850
Do you understand the importance of these ruins?

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.590
Your anger is marring an otherwise beautiful face.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.570
Don't fool around when I'm being serious.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.070
You sure are hard on us, missy.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.620
I haven't finished my investigation here.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.990
You're just in my way.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.700
Why, that's good news.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.670
We might find ourselves some treasures here.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.620
Have you heard a thing I said?

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.690
Okay now, let's all calm down.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.270
Our objectives may be different, but our methods are the same.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:05.550
Let's cooperate for now.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.050
Don't you start making excuses for your own benefit.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:14.350
In any case, until my investigation is over, please refrain from looting the ruins.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.270
You understand me?

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.850
W-What was that just now?

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.980
That was very intimidating.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.780
Why, good afternoon.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.020
Are you here for the same reasons we are?

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.280
Or are you here for a picnic?

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.940
We aren't!

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:36.290
Our job includes investigating these ruins.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.430
Which means...

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.790
You are officials from the branch?

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:40.930
Yes!

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:45.840
By the way, the lady just now said you two are ruin raiders?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.050
Shall we talk about that at the branch office?

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.090
Hang on, that's just a joke.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.730
I'm Reyfer, a treasure hunter.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:58.070
I'm the Honorary President of the
Self-Governing Body of Riesengang,

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.560
the Honorary President of Rare Item Enthusiasts Society,

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:06.900
the Assistant Deputy Director of the Colseit Friends, and famed adventurer, Harry Olsen.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.510
We truly aren't ruin raiders.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.160
May I see your badge as proof then?

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:13.240
Badge?

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:18.620
If you are working with the branch, you should have received a badge.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.080
Oh, that's right. The badge.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.170
I think we forgot ours at the inn.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.090
That's our mistake.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:30.360
We should go back to town first, Reyfer-kun.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.210
Exactly as you say, Boss.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:32.790
Later!

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:33.930
Be safe!

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.100
Oh, it's you.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:37.920
Hey!

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:38.810
See you later.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.210
What a bunch of strange people.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.770
Are they really not ruin raiders?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:54.150
Is damaging the ruins such a bad thing?

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.150
What's the matter?

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.160
Hey, Nio.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.870
Nio-san, what's the problem?

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:11.470
Actually, I have a sister who's also on a journey.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.230
Really?

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.720
And my sister is...

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:17.720
Well, she's being chased by people from Central City.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:19.970
What did she do?

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.930
She destroyed a ruin.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.710
No way.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:26.290
She didn't take anything.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.650
It's just that she wanted to investigate a really big ruin,

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:35.210
so she continued to go deeper and deeper even though it was forbidden, and caused it to collapse.

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:38.580
The precious ruin was reduced to rubble.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:42.710
She'd go wherever her interests took her.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.040
She didn't mean to.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.830
It just turned out that way.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:49.660
We are government officials.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:53.340
We can't turn a blind eye if we come across a person wanted by Central City.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.870
Logy-san!

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:55.720
Why you!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:59.070
I suppose you're right.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:02.730
But if she runs away beforehand, there's nothing we can do about it.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:07.840
Just find your sister and run before we catch you.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.230
Which means...!

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.530
Thank you!

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:14.650
How did this conversation end on such a good note?

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.410
Are you ruin raiders?

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:28.570
I see, you two are from the Colseit Branch.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:29.380
Yes!

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:33.510
I'm Threia Hazelgrimm, an archaeologist.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.980
I mainly investigate ancient ruins.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:38.390
I have permission.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.830
So you're an archaeologist.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:44.890
About that, I picked up a stone tablet yesterday.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.450
I wonder which era this is from.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.270
I'll hold onto it and analyse it later.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.070
Yes, please.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:56.310
So what are you doing here?

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:01.530
The water flowing out of the ruins has been dirty lately, so we're here to investigate.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:06.040
True, the water doesn't look good.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.820
We must head further inside to find out.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.110
It's bright.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.930
These ruins are still alive.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.730
Wilbell-san said that earlier too.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.690
There are ruins like this all over.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:38.110
Long ago, there was a very advanced civilisation with powerful alchemic knowledge.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.990
It doesn't exist anymore, does it?

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:44.790
That's right, but the ruins they created were left behind.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:49.040
And there are a few among them that remain alive, such as this one.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:57.830
In other words, the ruins still retain their original functionality.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.350
Nio, do you hear anything?

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.140
Nope.

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:18.780
This is probably the centre.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.250
Look!

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.370
Look! That's where the water's coming from.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.770
The rocks are in the way.

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:36.800
I can hear her.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:38.740
Nio-san?

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:39.720
What did she say?

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:44.140
"Don't wake me up."

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:46.140
"Don't wake me up"?

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.680
What's going on?

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:53.570
It's no good.

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:54.770
It won't open!

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:00.320
Look over there!

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:15.830
It's coming this way!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.890
No effect?!

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:32.550
It's an Alchemical creature.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.420
Alchemical creature?

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:39.530
They're artificial creatures created using
sophisticated alchemy by past civilisations.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.860
Immortal beings that do not fall ill or age.

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:45.160
Normal weapons won't work.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.370
What should we do?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.970
Alchemical creatures?

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:54.370
Immortality?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:13:01.590
Something like that stands no chance against me,
the great and invincible mage, Wilbell voll-Erslied-sama!

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:04.220
A pumpkin?!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.680
Take this!

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:21.690
You defeated it?

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:23.670
How was that?

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:26.490
Did you see my great magic?

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:29.200
All I saw was you throwing a pumpkin.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.450
That's magic.

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:35.090
What's wrong with you, making such a fuss?

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:37.120
Huh?

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:52.790
You've only made the situation worse!

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:54.790
I'll throw another one!

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:05.110
Wilbell-san, how about a different spell?

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.650
I don't have time to cast right now!

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:10.070
If I could just close in...

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:20.040
Logy-san!

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.450
Linca-san!

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.450
Onii-chan?!

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:51.320
Linca?

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:58.870
You two...

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.830
Yo, Missy.

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:09.550
All right! Let's do it!

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.830
Are you okay, Logy-san?

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.380
Yeah, I'm fine,

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:35.370
but why are Linca-san and Awin...?

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:36.620
Linca!

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:41.000
Hold him off for ten seconds!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.150
Ten seconds.

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.130
Here I go!

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:49.260
I call upon our ancient contract passed down through the ages.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:54.720
Let my voice transcend the gap between the present and the past to deliver these words.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:16:02.190
Under the laws of this boundless world which serve all living beings, I summon thee.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.520
Thou art softer than strings, yet stronger than steel.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:10.070
Thy power revitalises land, melts ice, and extinguishes flames.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:14.320
Answer my call and appear before me, the Lord of Wind!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.610
Do it!

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:50.440
How's that?!

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.280
Amazing.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:56.530
Did she get it?

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.450
It can still move, huh?

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:04.610
Wilbell-san!

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:06.170
I can't use that magic consecutively!

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:12.350
Um, I...

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:16.430
I brought a few of these for protection.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:19.630
Just throw it and see how it goes!

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:20.180
Yes!

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.170
What the hell?!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.930
What the?

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.620
How dangerous.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:50.590
The flow is being impeded by this rock.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:07.230
Water!

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:16.470
There shouldn't be any more problems with the village's water now.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:17.110
Yeah.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:19.480
I don't know about that.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:21.560
What's wrong?

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:27.390
The ruins can pump clean water from deep underground.

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:31.340
However, it's apparent the water isn't flowing as fast as it used to.

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:35.130
That's why it was so easily impeded in the first place.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.880
So does that mean this will likely happen again?

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:39.890
Probably.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.850
I see.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:46.460
We'll just resupply them when necessary.

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:47.810
Using that.

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:51.060
It's the balloon!

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:52.850
You fixed it!

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:56.350
Yeah, and when I was coming to bring more supplies,

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:58.820
Linca-san came with me, saying she wanted to help you two.

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:02.070
I wanted to repay you for giving me food.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:04.110
Linca-san!

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:10.000
And when we arrived in the village,
those two told us you went to the ruins.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.580
So that's how!

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:14.540
I guess ruin raiders make themselves useful sometimes.

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:17.830
I told you, we are not ruin raiders.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:23.010
Okay, we're heading for Colseit.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:23.850
All aboard!

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:30.140
Um, is it okay if we come too?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:33.160
Yeah, you two helped Escha out, after all.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.620
Get on!

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.720
Thank you!

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.740
Thank you, Escha-san! Logy-san!

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.690
See ya!

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:43.660
Catch you later!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.620
We'll come again!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.290
Okay, we'll ride the winds!

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.860
Do you have a reason to visit Colseit?

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.190
Nio said she wanted to.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:22.030
I started hearing those mysterious voices only after I arrived here.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:26.010
I thought I might find out why if I visited Colseit.

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:26.950
I see.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.700
If you don't mind, you can stay at my home!

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:31.160
Thank you!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:34.960
Don't look down.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:40.090
Logy-san, are you okay?

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.440
Yeah, it's just an old scar.

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:43.880
Don't worry about it.

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:49.390
I wonder what will happen to the village.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:54.810
Even the advanced civilisation that built the ruins couldn't escape destruction.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:58.590
There's only so much we can do.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.270
True...

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:04.780
Even so, you want to help whenever you can, don't you?

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:07.220
Yes!

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:07.830
Look!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.310
It's Colseit!

